                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "There are four major issues with this game, in my opinion.\n\n1 - Running the game\nAfter reading multiple tutorials in order to run it, you will still encounter countless crashes. I lost progress so often I had to save about every minute. Crashes happened both on Steam Deck and PC.\n\n2 - The gameplay\nAs a creature capture game, it's mediocre. Most fights felt like a slog of fast forward and auto battle. Adding new creatures to your party feels awful, because as soon as you capture them, even at later dungeons, they come at level 1, so if you want to actually use them you probably need to grind. There are lots of places that are huge for no reason, and all you do is hold forward for a minute until you reach the next place.\n\n3 - The story\nMost Final Fantasy games focus heavily on the narrative aspect. I didn't expect a game that is trying to add creatures, characters and places from other worlds into one universe to have the same level of storytelling as the mainline series, but it was still a letdown.\n\n4 - The target audience\nWho is this game for exactly? It has a childish tone, full of jokes for kids, but at the same time it sells itself as a creature capturing game for people that played other Final Fantasy games to bathe in nostalgia. The original Final Fantasy was released in 1987, Final Fantasy VII was released almost 30 years ago. No kid has any nostalgia for those titles, so obviously only adults are playing this, yet it feels like the game is meant for 12 year olds at most. The credits roll scene with the chibi characters dancing almost feels like the game was actually made for toddlers. There's a complete disconnection from the game and its target audience.\n\n5 - DLC\nThere is a DLC for this game that every review it has will tell you the same thing: all of its content should have been in the base game. It's all quality of life with a little bit more content.\n\n6 - Achievements\nFortunately, no missable achievements here, just the combination of the worst most grindy achievements possible. The minigames were some of the worst I have ever played, and all of them had achievements involved.\n\nIn conclusion, this game is not for adults, it's for kids. Only get it if it's on sale.",
